**Convention 10.1 (literature attribution).** The finite sum-product,
equality elimination, bijection propagation, two-phase influence,
graph-partition and probabilistic graph ingredients are mature methods.
Their use here is within the explicit native bridges above, classified
as `repo-derived`. The cited primary statements below are
`literature-attested` intermediates or comparisons, not new native
results and not proofs of the unresolved optimized gap.

